<SnapshotIndexes Version="1.0" BinderUUID="AC58BF0A-5B02-4894-A652-44126004F905">
    <Snapshot Date="2026-11-06 16:24:52 -0800">
        <Title>Untitled Snapshot</Title>
        <Text>Research Question 3 (RQ3): Is there a connection between RBIs and player’s birth month? In other words, does the month the player was born in influence the total amount of RBIs in their career? To minimize data noise, only retired players will be analyzed for this question.
Hypothesis 3 (H3): The team believes there is a week correlation between RBIs and birth months for MLB players. There are multiple variables that affect a player’s rushing ability, including the birth location, or high school location elevation. Additionally, a player’s genetic makeup may influence oxygen saturation level (see, for example, Gibbens [2018] article on the Bajau’s people ability to stay underwater for up to 13 minutes without physical harm).
</Text>
    </Snapshot>
